**Planning CSS Overrides**

I see there are currently no CSS rules for the ant-card-head, so I need to plan on adding some. Since our earlier modifications to styles.css aren't affecting the cards due to the ant-dark algorithm, I propose we add CSS overrides with higher specificity and use !important under `.app-theme-dark` to ensure they take effect. I also want to make sure we address the grey requirement for ant-card-head and border colors, while considering the user's needs in our planning process.
**Creating CSS Override Plan**

I need to create a plan for overriding card head backgrounds and possibly other card backgrounds in dark mode since our earlier changes weren't sufficient. I won't call ApplyPatch yet because we can't edit directly. Instead, I'll focus on creating an updated plan with the CreatePlan tool. I believe I have enough information to proceed with this. I need to clarify whether to use `html.app-theme-dark` or just `.app-theme-dark` for the CSS rules. Let's draft the plan accordingly!
**Drafting CSS Rules**

I'll set the CSS rules to override the card backgrounds in dark mode. I'm thinking of using:

```css
html.app-theme-dark .ant-card {
  background: var(--bg-surface) !important;
}
html.app-theme-dark .ant-card-head {
  background: var(--bg-surface) !important;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle) !important;
}
html.app-theme-dark .ant-card-body {
  background: var(--bg-surface) !important; 
}
```

However, if the user prefers grey, I'll maintain that while ensuring any bordered cards default to the proper background. I'll also set the text color for `.ant-card-head-title` to var(--text-primary) to align with AntD's settings. This will ensure everything works smoothly for the user!
**Ensuring CSS Order**

I need to make sure the new CSS rules are properly ordered. I'll plan to add them near the bottom of styles.css, preferably after the variable definitions or possibly after the upload preview boxes—whichever ensures the right specificity. It might be helpful to create a plan with the CreatePlan tool. Also, I’m considering whether I should ask “why deep blue” since the ant-card-head uses a background token that we need to override. Let’s proceed with that plan!

